#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (Ti,V)O2 in the rutile structure (P 42/m n m, No. 136), written the way
# careless files are: operations only as a Hall symbol, Ti1 and O1 a few
# thousandths of an angstrom off their special positions, the Ti/V mixed
# site as two rows with slightly different coordinates, and O2 repeating
# O1 at an equivalent position. The importer snaps, merges and drops.
# Hand-written test fixture for Materials Workbench (mw-crystal-io).
# Values are commonly cited literature parameters, typed in by hand;
# nothing is copied from a database.
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

data_rutile_near_special
_chemical_formula_sum             'O2 Ti0.9 V0.1'
_space_group_name_H-M_alt         'P 42/m n m'
_space_group_name_Hall            '-P 4n 2n'
_cell_length_a                    4.594
_cell_length_b                    4.594
_cell_length_c                    2.959
_cell_angle_alpha                 90
_cell_angle_beta                  90
_cell_angle_gamma                 90

loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
_atom_site_occupancy
Ti1 Ti4+  0.0004  -0.0003  0.0002  0.9
V1  V4+   0        0       0       0.1
O1  O2-   0.3046   0.3050  0.0010  1
O2  O2-   0.6952   0.6952  0       1
